  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Electromotive force (e.m.f.) is the name given to the potential difference of the power source in a circuit\n- It is defined as **The electrical work done by a source in moving a unit charge around a complete circuit**\n- Electromotive force (e.m.f.) is measured in volts (V)"
  },
